IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga2-nouns`
IMPORT `sga2-s76-offence`

-- Tests for sga2-s76-offence.l4: s 76(5), (6) and (7) of the Companies Act 1967 (Singapore).
-- Expected values are written from the text (inputs/CoA1967.txt lines 7412-7434), beside each assertion.

§ `s 76(5): the offence of the officers in default`

-- "the company shall not be guilty of an offence": a flat negative where the company contravened (1) or (1A).
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the company is guilty of an offence by contravening subsection (1) or (1A)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No contravention: the sentence says nothing of the company.
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the company is guilty of an offence by contravening subsection (1) or (1A)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "each officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence": contravention, officer, in default.
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the officer is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both": 20000 dollars, 36 months, both.
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 20000, 36, TRUE)
-- A penalty one dollar or one month either side is not the text's.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76(5) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 20001, 36, TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 76(5) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 76 penalty` OF 20000, 35, TRUE))
-- The officer is not guilty: the subsection states no penalty for them.
#ASSERT `s 76(5) the most the officer may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The derived prohibition on the officer: being in default when the company contravenes is BREACH; no event is a standing prohibition.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 76(5) an officer of the company must not be in default when the company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)` "Tan Ah Kow" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY (Officer "Tan Ah Kow") DOES `s 76(5) be an officer of the company who is in default when the company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)` AT 4

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 76(5) an officer of the company must not be in default when the company contravenes subsection (1) or (1A)` "Tan Ah Kow" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 9)

§ `s 76(6): compensation on conviction`

-- "Where a person is convicted of an offence under subsection (5) and the Court ... is satisfied that the company or another person has suffered loss or damage": both.
#ASSERT `s 76(6) the Court may order the convicted person to pay compensation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(6) the Court may order the convicted person to pay compensation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(6) the Court may order the convicted person to pay compensation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76(6) the Court may order the convicted person to pay compensation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "any such order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court": an order under (6) only.
#ASSERT `s 76(6) the order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(6) the order may be enforced as if it were a judgment of the Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 76(7): relief under section 391`

#ASSERT `s 76(7) the power of the Court under section 391 extends to relieving the person from the liability to have an order made under subsection (6)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76(7) the power of the Court under section 391 extends to relieving the person from the liability to have an order made under subsection (6)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
